      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:3:5:2",
      "text": [
        " قَالَ أَبُو الْحَسَنِ ( عليه السلام ) إِذَا مَرِضَ أَحَدُكُمْ فَلْيَأْذَنْ لِلنَّاسِ يَدْخُلُونَ عَلَيْهِ فَإِنَّهُ لَيْسَ مِنْ أَحَدٍ إِلَّا وَ لَهُ دَعْوَةٌ مُسْتَجَابَةٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, from Ahmad Bin Muhammad Bin Isa, from Abdul Aziz Bin Muhtada, from Yunus who said, ",
          "‘Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘When one of you gets sick, so let him give permission to the people to come over to him, for there is no one except for him is an Answered supplication’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn ‘Isa from ‘Abd al-‘Aziz al-Muhtadiy from Yunus who has said the following: “Abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘If one of you becomes ill he should allow people to visit him; everyone’s prayer has a chance to receive acceptance.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
